course: dictionary
lesson: 8546
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word scale is a good example. In «The Lord detests dishonest scales», scales means a tool for weighing things. A scale can also be a set of marks for measuring, like on a ruler.
explain: Read the words around the word. In «A large-scale map, such as 1:25,000, shows a small area in great detail», the words large-scale and great detail tell you that scale is about how much of the real world a map shows and how small it is made. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Scale can also be a verb, an action word. «To scale a wall» means to climb it. Its forms are scale, scales, scaled and scaling, so the sentence around it still gives the clue about what is happening.
fact: A scale can be a tool for weighing things, such as kitchen scales.
fact: On a map, the scale shows how real distances are made smaller: «1 cm stands for 1 km».
fact: Scales are also the small hard plates on the skin of fish and snakes.
fact: A scale in music is a set of notes going up or down in order.
fact: «To scale» a wall means to climb it.
exercise: «The Lord detests dishonest scales, but accurate weights find favour with him.» In this sentence, what are scales? | *A tool for weighing things | To climb up something | A set of notes going up or down | Small hard plates on a fish
exercise: «A large-scale map, such as 1:25,000, shows a small area in great detail.» What does this map show? | The notes of a song | A huge area with very little detail | The skin of a snake | *A small area in great detail
exercise: «To scale a wall» means what? | To paint it | *To climb it | To count its bricks
test: «1 cm stands for 1 km» is written on a map. What does the word scale mean here? | A tool for weighing the map | To climb the map | *How real distances are made smaller on paper | The small plates on a fish
test: «A scale on a thermometer» has marks with numbers. Which meaning of scale is this? | A tool for weighing things | A set of notes going up or down | To climb a wall | *A set of marks with numbers for measuring
exam: In «A self-checkout scanner reads barcodes, and a scale checks the weight of each item», which meaning of scale fits? | To climb up something | Small hard plates on the skin | A set of marks for measuring distance | *A tool for weighing things
